.TH KERNEL-PANIC-DETECTOR 1 "November 2026" "0.1.0" "Kernel Fault Lab Manual"
.SH NAME
kernel-panic-detector \- DKMS fault-injection kernel module (panic_lab) and monitor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sudo modprobe panic_lab
.br
.B dkms status
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B kernel-panic-detector
packages the \fBpanic_lab\fR Linux kernel module via DKMS to exercise and observe
kernel fault conditions such as memory leaks, race conditions, divide-by-zero,
and invalid memory dereferences alongside user-space monitoring.
.SH USAGE
Load and inspect the module with standard kernel utilities:
.TP
.B sudo modprobe panic_lab
Insert the compiled module into the running kernel.
.TP
.B sudo dmesg -w
Stream kernel ring-buffer messages and fault diagnostics.
.TP
.B sudo modprobe -r panic_lab
Unload the module cleanly when finished.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dkms (8),
.BR modprobe (8),
.BR dmesg (1)
